rses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And the LORD said unto Moses, Thus thou shalt say unto the children of Israel, Ye have seen that I have talked with you from heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVYe shall not make with me gods of silver, neither shall ye make unto you gods of gold.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙâAn altar of earth thou shalt make unto me, and shalt sacrifice thereon thy burnt offerings, and thy peace offerings, thy sheep, and thine oxen: in all places where I record my name I will come unto thee, and I will bless thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd if thou wilt make me an altar of stone, thou shalt not build it of hewn stone: for if thou lift up thy tool upon it, thou hast polluted it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Neither shalt thou go up by steps unto mine altar, that thy nakedness be not discovered thereon.¦layout ªlast_verse